                <pb facs="0936" n="927" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg927"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.5151/462: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-21T11:00:00-03:00">January 21, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 21—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. Import quotas of 11 countries have been increased by 50 per cent and British
                    by 250 per cent but United States still excluded. Exchange Control says value of
                    American merchandise blocked in Montevideo customhouse without quota is 1½
                    million dollars.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
